Under the BCERS alternatives consultant RFP, the **quarterly performance report must include, at a minimum**:

- A market overview and outlook;
- An allocation breakdown by geography, strategy, and industry;
- An update on each fund and a listing of funds by strategy;
- For each fund: commitment date and amount, drawdowns, outstanding commitment, distributions, net asset value, IRR, and multiples; and
- Aggregates of the drawdown, outstanding-commitment, distribution, net-asset-value, IRR, and multiple figures for the core private equity portfolio, the specialized portfolio, and the combined portfolio.

The quarterly report must also be reconciled with the BCERS custodian bank’s records. [Source: BCERS Alternatives Consultant RFP, pp. 6–7](Baltimore_BCERS__RFP-Alternatives-Consultant-rev.pdf).
